quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  3,141,And so that Allah may refine the believers (by testing them through their patience and steadfastness) and destroy the disbelievers (through their arrogance and transgression).
  3,142,"Do you assume that you will enter Paradise while Allah has not yet revealed those of you who have struggled hard (for His cause), nor has He revealed the steadfast?"
  3,143,"Certainly, you used to desire death (as a martyr) before you encountered it, and now you have seen it while you were looking on."
  3,144,"And Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) is but a Messenger; (other) messengers have (also) gone before him. If he were to die or be killed, would you turn back on your heels (towards disbelief)? Anyone who turns back on his heels will not harm Allah whatsoever. And Allah will soon reward the grateful (for remaining steadfast during hardship)."
  3,145,"It is not for a soul to die except with the permission of Allah at an appointed time. Whoever desires the reward of this world, We will give him of it. And whoever desires the reward of the Hereafter, We will give him of it. And We will soon reward the grateful."
  3,146,"And how many a prophet has been, while many godly devotees fought alongside them, who did not lose heart in the face of their sufferings in Allah’s cause; they neither weakened nor surrendered (or humbled themselves). And Allah loves the patient (and steadfast)."
  3,147,All that they would say was: ‘Our Lord! Forgive us our sins and our excesses in our affairs; keep our feet firm; and help us against the disbelieving people.’
  3,148,"Therefore, Allah gave them the reward of this world and the excellent reward of the Hereafter. And Allah loves those who are excellent (in devotion and steadfastness)."
